build(ch, "electricity", "Electricity: series circuits, conductors and safety", 35,
      ["Build and describe a series circuit.", "Say what happens when more bulbs are added.", "Know where electricity comes from and how to be safe."],
      [("key", "definition", "Circuits", "A **circuit** is a complete loop through which electricity flows. In a **series circuit** the parts (cell, switch, bulbs) are in **one loop**. If one bulb breaks, the loop is broken and **all the bulbs go out**. If you add more bulbs to one cell, each bulb is **dimmer**. A **switch** opens or closes the circuit."),
       ("fig", fig, "A series circuit with a cell and two bulbs.", "A single loop of wire with a cell on the left and two bulbs in a row at the top. The note says series circuit: one loop."),
       ("key", "retenir", "Conductors and sources", "**Conductors** (copper, iron, aluminium, graphite) let electricity pass; **insulators** (plastic, rubber, glass, dry wood) do not. Wires are copper covered with plastic for safety. Electricity can come from **cells**, from **generators**, from **solar panels** and from **dams** on rivers such as the Sanaga that drive generators."),
       ("key", "attention", "Safety", "**Never** touch bare wires or sockets. **Never** use electrical things with wet hands or near water. Do not pull a plug by its cable. Keep away from fallen cables and **tell an adult**. At school use only **small cells** and a teacher present, never the mains."),
       ("key", "pieges", "Common mistakes", "- Thinking that electricity is 'used up' by a bulb: the energy changes into light and heat, the current goes round.\n- Believing that more cells always means a dimmer bulb: more cells make it brighter, more bulbs make each dimmer.\n- Using a wet hand to switch on a light.\n- Thinking that all metals are safe to touch near power lines.")],
      [("ex", "Example 1", "In a series circuit with two bulbs, one bulb breaks. What happens to the other one?", ["The break stops the flow round the single loop.", "The other bulb also goes out."], "It goes out, because the circuit is broken.", None),
       ("ex", "Example 2", "A circuit with one cell and one bulb has a second bulb added in series. What happens to the brightness?", ["The same energy from the cell now lights two bulbs.", "Each bulb is dimmer."], "Each bulb is dimmer.", fig)],
      [M("application", "Which material is a good conductor of electricity?", "copper", ["rubber", "plastic", "dry wood"], "Metals conduct."),
       M("application", "What does a switch do?", "opens or closes the circuit", ["makes electricity", "makes light only", "cools the wire"], "It controls the flow."),
       M("application", "Why are wires covered in plastic?", "plastic is an insulator, so it is safe", ["plastic makes the wire hotter", "plastic is a conductor", "it makes the cell stronger"], "Insulation protects people."),
       TF("approfondissement", "In a series circuit, if one bulb breaks all the bulbs go out.", True, "The loop is broken."),
       MA("approfondissement", "Match each material with a type.", [("copper", "conductor"), ("rubber", "insulator"), ("sunlight on a panel", "a source of electricity (solar)"), ("a dam", "a source of electricity (water power)")], "Properties and sources."),
       P("Neba builds a series circuit with one cell and three bulbs. The bulbs are dim. His sister says he should use mains electricity to make them brighter.",
         [PM("Why are the bulbs dim?", "three bulbs share the energy of one cell", ["the wire is too long", "the bulbs are cold", "the cell is full"], "More bulbs mean dimmer bulbs."),
          PM("How can Neba make them brighter safely?", "use fewer bulbs or add another small cell", ["connect them to the mains", "use a wet hand", "use a bare wire in a socket"], "Safe changes only."),
          PM("Why is her idea dangerous?", "mains electricity can hurt or kill", ["mains is cold", "it is slow", "it does not light bulbs"], "Never use mains for experiments.", points=2)])],
      [("A series circuit has...", "one loop", ["two loops", "no wires", "no cell"], "All parts in a single loop."),
       ("An insulator...", "does not let electricity pass", ["lets electricity pass", "makes electricity", "is always metal"], "Plastic, rubber."),
       ("Which is an electricity source?", "a cell", ["a stone", "a stick", "a cloth"], "Also generators and solar panels."),
       ("Which is a safety rule?", "never touch sockets with wet hands", ["touch bare wires", "pull plugs by the cable", "use mains for experiments"], "Water and electricity are dangerous."),
       ("If a bulb breaks in a series circuit, the other bulbs...", "go out", ["shine brighter", "stay the same", "turn blue"], "The loop is broken.")],
      ["Safety rules and experiments must be supervised by a teacher; a parallel circuit is not covered."])

